First perform hostile technical verification. Trace the actual production code and try to disprove attacker control, reachability, the missing guard, and the claimed terminal effect. Do not carry a candidate forward merely because it is plausible.

As a new verifier, try to disprove {{dedup_canonical_hypothesis_id}}. Reconstruct authentication -> subject/tenant derivation -> object loading -> authorization -> state transition -> terminal effect across middleware, services, jobs, and downstream checks. Prove control over each identifier, field, timing, and prerequisite state. Inspect ownership, tenancy, policy caching, idempotency, database constraints, isolation/locking, transactions, rollback, feature flags, and alternate guards. supported requires a complete production path and concrete cross-boundary or security-sensitive effect; otherwise falsified/blocked. Produce a minimal isolated multi-account reproduction plan.

If and only if the technical verdict remains supported, immediately attempt the smallest safe deterministic reproduction in this same job. A failed or blocked reproduction must be recorded honestly; it must not erase a technically supported candidate that still needs manual validation.

For supported candidates, reproduce in an authorized isolated environment with the smallest stateful sequence and at least two principals/tenants when relevant. Capture identities/roles, object ownership, requests/events, before/after state, response and downstream effect. Prefer an integration/regression test and repeat the decisive sequence. Respect {{extra.authorized_test_constraints}}. Set PoC verdict and preserve commands, evidence, artifacts, minimal reproduction, and assumptions.

For smart-contract candidates, use {{extra.fork_rpc_url}} and {{extra.fork_block}} when supplied. Never send transactions to a public network.

Do not apply the bounty-program eligibility decision and do not write the final finding in this step. Populate every verify_* and poc_* field. Use technical_verdict=falsified when the code contradicts the hypothesis, blocked only for a specific missing fact or unavailable environment, and supported only for a complete code-grounded path.

Apply the immutable bounty-program evidence to one independently checked candidate, then emit its progressive finding record.

